.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA ,
.Nm EVP_KEYMGMT-SLH-DSA ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-192s ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-192f ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-256s ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-256f ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128s ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128f ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-192s ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-192f ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256s ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256f
.Nd EVP_PKEY SLH-DSA keytype and algorithm support
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Sy SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f ,
.Sy SLH-DSA-SHA2-192s ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-192f ,
.Sy SLH-DSA-SHA2-256s ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHA2-256f ,
.Sy SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128s ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128f ,
.Sy SLH-DSA-SHAKE-192s ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-192f ,
.Sy SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256s
and
.Sy EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256f
key types are implemented in OpenSSL's default and FIPS providers.
These implementations support the associated key, containing the public
key
.Em pub
and the private key
.Em priv .
.Pp
SLH-DSA (Stateless Hash-based Digital Signature Standard) uses small
keys, but has relatively large signatures and is relatively slow
performing all operations compared to
.Sy ML-DSA .
It does however have proven security proofs, since it relies only on
hash functions.
.Pp
Each of the different key types has an associated security parameter
.Sy n .
This value is one of 16, 24 or 32 for key types
.Sy SLH-DSA*128* ,
.Sy SLH-DSA*192*
and
.Sy SLH-DSA*256* ,
respectively.
.Pp
Both the public and private key components contain 2 elements of size
.Sy n .
Key generation generates the private key elements and one of the public
key elements randomly, and the final public key element is computed from
these values.
.Pp
The public key has relatively small sizes of 32, 48 or 64 bytes,
corresponding to the algorithm names of 128, 192 and 256 respectively.
.Pp
The algorithms ending with
.Sy s
produce smaller signatures, but are much slower than the faster
.Sy f
variants.
.Pp
The signature sizes for the
.Sy s
algorithm variants are 7856, 16224 and 29792 which correspond to the
algorithm names of 128s, 192s and 256s respectively.
The signature sizes for the
.Sy f
algorithm variants are 17088, 35664 and 49856 which correspond to the
algorithm names containing 128f, 192f and 256f respectively.
.Pp
Internally there are 7 hash related functions that are used for each
algorithm.
For algorithms containing
.Sy SHAKE
in their name
.Sy SHAKE-256
is used for all functions.
For the <SHA2-128> algorithms the functions use <MGF1-SHA-256>,
<HMAC-SHA-256> and <SHA-256>. The remaining <SHA2> algorithms use
<MGF1-SHA-512>, <HMAC-SHA-512>, <SHA-256> and <SHA-512>. See FIPS 205
Section 11.1 and 11.2 for more information.
.Ss Keygen Parameters
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqseed" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_SLH_DSA_SEED Ns ) <octet string>
Supplies values to use for the private seed, private prf and public seed
instead of generating random values.
This is used for testing purposes only.
The length of the value supplied must be 3 *
.Sy n .
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <utf8_string>
Sets properties to be used when fetching algorithm implementations used
for SLH-DSA hashing operations.
.El
.Pp
Use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3
after calling
.Xr EVP_PKEY_keygen_init 3 .
.Ss Common SLH-DSA parameters
In addition to the common parameters that all keytypes should support
(see
.Xr provider-keymgmt 7 Ns ),
the implementation of these key types support the following.
.Pp
The following parameters are gettable using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param 3 ,
and settable when using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_fromdata 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqpub" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PUB_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
The public key has a size of 2 *
.Sy n
bytes.
i.e.
It consists of the concatenation of PK.seed and PK.root as defined by
FIPS 205 Figure 16.
.It \(dqpriv" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PRIV_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
The private key has a size of 4 *
.Sy n
bytes, which includes the public key components.
i.e.
It consists of the concatenation of SK.seed, SK.prf, PK.seed and PF.root
as defined by FIPS 205 Figure 15.
.It \(dqmandatory-digest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_MANDATORY_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
The empty string, signifying that no digest may be specified.
.El
.Sh CONFORMING TO
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It FIPS 205
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
An
.Sy EVP_PKEY
context can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
    EVP_PKEY_CTX *pctx =
        EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name(NULL, "SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f", NULL);
.Ed
.Pp
An
.Sy SLH-DSA
key can be generated like this:
.Bd -literal
    pkey = EVP_PKEY_Q_keygen(NULL, NULL, "SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f");
.Ed
.Pp
The key pair components can be extracted from a key by calling:
.Bd -literal
    uint8_t priv[64], pub[32];
    size_t priv_len, pub_len;

    EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param(pkey, OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PRIV_KEY,
                                    priv, sizeof(priv), &priv_len);
    EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param(pkey, OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PUB_KEY,
                                    pub, sizeof(pub), &pub_len));
.Ed
.Pp
Similar code can be used for the other key types such as
"SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256f".
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_KEYMGMT 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY 3 ,
.Xr provider-keymgmt 7 ,
.Xr EVP_SIGNATURE-SLH-DSA 7
